«
@@ ============================================================
@@ μ♁StdAtm — Earth dynamic viscosity, USSA 1976 temperature + Sutherland's law (homosphere ≤86 km)
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@
@@ Input  : Z   ( geometric altitude, length unit e.g. 50_km )
@@ Output : see units below
@@ VALIDATION (device / double-precision):
@@   2000_m μ♁StdAtm -> 1.7259816E-5 Pa·s ; 60_km -> 1.5837189E-5 Pa·s (device)
@@ ============================================================
@Earth: U.S. Standard Atmosphere Viscosity Profile: μ♁StdAtm(Z_m); Z_m: geometric height
@Source: USSA 1976 temperature + Sutherland's law
@(https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/stp/space-weather/online-publications/miscellaneous/us-standard-atmosphere-1976/us-standard-atmosphere_st76-1562_noaa.pdf)
@Validity domain: Zmin=-5000_m; Zmax=86000_m
@covering Troposphere (0-11_km) Stratosphere (11-47_km) & Mesosphere (47-86_km)
→ Z
  «
    Z 1_m Convert 'Z' Store
    Z UnitValue 86000 <
    if
    then
      Z T♁StdAtm UnitValue             @ Extract pure value of T_K (ex: 275.154)
      Duplicate 1.5 ^ 1.458E-6 ×       @ Calculation of beta × T^(3/2)
      Swap 110.4 +               @ Calculation of T + S
      ÷                          @ Dividing both terms
     1_Pa*s ×                   @ Attach units of dynamic viscosity
    else
      "Z out of range -5000_m < Z < 86000_m" DoError
    end
  »
»
